WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:11.760
Hey, what's up guys it's Rob and welcome
to my tutorial for: The Ninja Star

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:15.150
Boomerang! I spoke with Jeremy Shafer about trying

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.390
to come up with a ninja star that comes
back and while each of us were trying to

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.840
figure it out, we both came up with our
own designs. Mine is made from half a

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:35.670
sheet of printer paper and flies like
this... while Jeremy's is made from for

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:40.770
origami squares and flies just like this.
I'll have a link to his tutorial at the

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:43.800
end of the video so be sure to check it
out! I'm really happy and proud of the

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.410
Ninja Star Boomerang because it's not
only easy to make, but it flies

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:49.649
incredibly well. Better than any
boomerang that I've made and has quickly

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:52.559
become my favorite thing to make. You're
gonna want to show it off to all your

00:00:52.559 --> 00:00:56.080
friends, so be sure to give it a thumbs
up down below if you do enjoy the video!

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:59.579
So grab your piece of paper and let's
make it! For the tutorial we're going to

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:03.420
need half a sheet of letter size printer
paper just like this which we'll then

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.710
split up again into quarters and make
two identical pieces which will then fit

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:12.330
together and interlock just like the
ninja stars - I highly recommend you

00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:15.869
first try with a plain white sheet
because although it looks a little nicer

00:01:15.869 --> 00:01:20.220
with the colored paper, I found out the
white is a little bit thinner and winds

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:24.570
up flying much better. We can first fold
the paper in half by taking the top and

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.619
aligning it with the bottom and once
it's lined up neatly we can make a nice

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:31.470
sharp crease along the top with our
fingernail

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:35.850
by running it across a couple times and
you can either cut it or as I prefer to

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:40.409
do just tear it right in half. To split
the paper into quarters we can do the

00:01:40.409 --> 00:01:44.070
same exact thing by folding the paper in
half and meeting the edges together

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:48.329
neatly then we can make a nice sharp
crease along the top and just carefully

00:01:48.329 --> 00:01:52.530
rip the paper in half. Now that we have
the paper in quarters like we need, we

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:56.159
can go on to make the two units and
interlock them. So, just set one of the

00:01:56.159 --> 00:01:59.909
pieces aside and then we're going to
take the quarter and we're going to fold

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:05.460
it in half. So just align the edges
together, once it's neatly aligned just

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:11.970
make a crease all throughout the paper
and just give it a nice sharp crease on

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.970
top.  Now we can take the left side and fold

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:21.400
it across to the right side, line up the
two ends and just give it a hold here on

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:27.220
the right and a tug in the middle and
crease it on the left side. Just run your

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.090
fingernail against it once and then you
could open it up so that it's a mountain

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.980
fold and that the open edges are on the
bottom. Set it down and I'm just going to

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:39.910
mark it so that you can see it a little
easier here. Now, we could take the right

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:43.300
side and we're just going to take this
top edge and fold it down onto that

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:49.000
vertical line give it a nice crease here
and on the left side we're just going to

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.970
do the opposite so we're gonna take the
bottom and fold it up. Once we do that, we

00:02:54.970 --> 00:02:59.680
can then crease on that new fold so you
should have something like this and

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.769
we're just going to flip it over and
just make sure that it's nice and flat.

00:03:04.769 --> 00:03:08.440
These next folds we're going to make are
important because it's going to

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:13.390
establish the flap or the sort of little
"Air Foil" that we have here on each of the

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:18.310
wings or arms the boomerang that help
it fly in that nice circle. We're going

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:24.070
to fold this top edge down to the bottom
just like this, except we're not going to

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:27.400
fold it all the way. We're going to leave
a little bit of space and as you'll see

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:32.019
here, I've made a mark and that mark is
one-eighth of an inch from the bottom.

00:03:32.019 --> 00:03:36.459
I'm giving you a measurement because
I think you should probably try it the

00:03:36.459 --> 00:03:40.959
first time you make it just so you have
an idea of about how much that is. And as

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:46.180
you'll see here on the ruler, an eighth
of an inch is just basically that first

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:51.280
big increment that we have right here.
Now that you know what to do we're going

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.780
to take the edge and we're just going to
fold it like this and as you'll see the

00:03:55.780 --> 00:04:00.160
whole left side comes along. I'm just
going to basically line it up with that

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.560
line that I drew so this whole left side
should kind of flip and I'm going to

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:12.130
line it up all the way across and then
make a nice sharp crease. Now, I'm going

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:16.570
to just run my fingernail against the
top. Now, we're going to do the same on

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:21.780
the other side so all we need to do is
to flip it upside down like this and

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:26.680
then we're going to take this edge right
here and we're going to

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:30.610
fold it down as well leaving a little
bit of space-- about an eighth of an inch.

00:04:30.610 --> 00:04:33.970
I'm going to eyeball at this time but if
you want to draw the line from the

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:40.750
bottom you can. Just take it and fold it
down like this leaving a little bit of

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:46.300
space and make sure that it's parallel
all the way across. Once you have it

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:51.789
pretty even all the way on the bottom,
then you can make that crease on top and

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:56.740
just give it a nice good crease and make
sure that you didn't kind of pull these

00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:02.039
apart. So it should look something like
this.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:09.400
Now that we made those folds, you'll see
on the front here I have a diamond that

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:13.990
I'm holding facing towards me whereas on
the back it's split where we folded

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:18.849
those two edges. I'm going to
basically take the ends here and I'm

00:05:18.849 --> 00:05:23.800
just going to hold them like this with
the corners facing towards me I'm going

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:29.320
to open them now I'm going to airplane
both of the corners into this vertical

00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:34.680
line just like this. So just fold it
directly on that vertical line here and

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:40.270
make a crease and then do the same on
the left side. As you'll see, because the

00:05:40.270 --> 00:05:45.849
left side is thinner it makes a smaller
triangle but we both want these top

00:05:45.849 --> 00:05:52.090
edges directly on the middle just like
that. Then you can re-close the two edges

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:58.419
together and just pinch it and make a
crease do the same on the other side.

00:05:58.419 --> 00:06:05.110
Just hold it like this open it up and
just airplane these corners directly on

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:12.130
to the center and then re-close it so it
should look something like this. Now all

00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:16.180
we need to do now is basically just fold
these arms in a little bit-- it's not

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:21.340
critically important where it is usually
right around this little point or corner

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:24.550
that you see right here. So I'm just
going to take it and just fold it like

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:28.270
this and you'll feel some resistance so
right when you feel some resistance

00:06:28.270 --> 00:06:31.870
right around there is good and we're
just going to make sure that this

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:37.150
outside edge is aligned with this one on
the bottom so once they're lined up like

00:06:37.150 --> 00:06:40.270
this. Then you could just give it a good
pinch.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:45.190
Then you can unfold it and you can do
the same with the left side so just take

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:50.110
it like this and just lift it up and
fold it across and when you feel some

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:55.180
resistance, right around this corner here,
then all you need to do is to just line

00:06:55.180 --> 00:06:59.139
it up and just give it a pinch. And there
you go! That's how to make one of the

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:04.180
pieces. Now that we've finished the first
piece, the second piece is made the same

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:07.900
exact way. So if you need to you can
re-watch the time that I've listed below

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.560
and when you're done we're ready to
interlock the two pieces together.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:15.159
Alright guys, all that's left now is to
interlock the two pieces together and as

00:07:15.159 --> 00:07:19.960
you'll see I'm holding them so that the
diamonds are facing me on the right side.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.860
I drew a line from the top of the
diamond to the bottom and on the left

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:27.729
side I drew one from the left to the
right. We're basically just going to

00:07:27.729 --> 00:07:33.130
take the one on the right and turn it 90
degrees and put it on top of the one on

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:36.430
the left. And if you can see, you're just going to

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:40.569
basically overlap the diamonds by kind
of putting them right in the middle and

00:07:40.569 --> 00:07:43.419
sort of overlapping the lines just like
that.

00:07:43.419 --> 00:07:48.820
So right around there is good. I'm going
to start with the top arm and we're

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:53.409
going to fold it down and we're going to
go in a clockwise direction. So that's

00:07:53.409 --> 00:07:59.199
one, then we go here that's two. You
can move these around if you need to

00:07:59.199 --> 00:08:03.520
because they are going to start
overlapping. So here we go this is three.

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.380
As you'll see if it gets a little
scrunched up then you just can move move

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:15.250
it around like this. Shift this down the
last one here is going to go over this

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:20.259
one the third one and underneath the
first one kind of under here. So what I'm

00:08:20.259 --> 00:08:24.400
going to do is hold it here and I'm
going to lift up the first one by just

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:29.229
pulling it out like this. I'm gonna
pinch it right here and I'm going to

00:08:29.229 --> 00:08:33.880
take the last arm and just round it off
a little bit and then I'm going to stick

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:39.539
the point right into that opening right
there and I'm going to pull it through.

00:08:39.539 --> 00:08:43.450
Now, when you pull these through you want
to make sure that they go up to the

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:48.310
folds that you kind of created before. So
you want to reach up the first one that

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:52.480
you pulled out just like this kind of
push it in.

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:57.520
While you're pushing in the other ones
like this and make sure that it's nice

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:01.120
and flat in the middle. You can kind of tug on the opposite ones

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:05.890
a little bit like this, and there you go!
You'll see it will come together sort of

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:09.490
like that. So just make sure it's nice
and flat in the middle once you get it

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:13.060
all interlocked. Then all we need to do is

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:17.860
basically take this little
overlap this little flap and we're going

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:24.100
to fold it right along this edge so just
take it and fold it right all the way

00:09:24.100 --> 00:09:27.250
down I'm going to set it down on the
table because it's a little easier for

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:33.040
me. Just gonna take the edge and fold it
all the way down on there as you'll

00:09:33.040 --> 00:09:38.320
notice when you do that it doesn't want
to fold in the corner here, that's okay.

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:42.970
You just need to leave it a little bit
curved. So just press it like

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.860
that right in the corner then just
rotate it fold this one down now all the

00:09:47.860 --> 00:09:56.530
way. Then the next one fold it down and
just walk my finger up right there and

00:09:56.530 --> 00:10:02.200
then finally we'll do the last one.
There you go there is your ninja star

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:06.790
boomerang. Now what I like to do is to
just run my fingernail over all of the

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:13.750
creases especially these right here you
want to make sure it's nice and flat. So

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:19.990
just press it down like this upside down
and you're ready to throw it! I'm going

00:10:19.990 --> 00:10:24.010
to hold the boomerang so that the four
interlocked boxes are facing the left

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:28.870
side with the air foils and my pointer
and middle finger are grabbing one of

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:33.100
the arms just like this close to the end.
I'm going to rest the

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:37.780
other arm of the boomerang on my palm
right near my thumb like this, and I'm

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:42.220
going to basically curl my wrist and I'm
going to flick it out like that like I

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:46.360
would with a yo-yo. You could do it
directly out but I also recommend you

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:50.710
can do it up like this at like a
twenty or thirty degree angle. Alright so

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:54.700
I'm just gonna basically go like this
and flick my wrist really hard and

00:10:54.700 --> 00:11:00.120
release the boomerang. Okay so let's give
it a shot!

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:27.639
Thank you guys so much for watching my
tutorial for my all-new Ninja Star

00:11:27.639 --> 00:11:31.540
Boomerang design if you did like it
don't forget to give it a thumbs up down

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:34.930
below and if you're not already
subscribed click that subscribe and

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:38.680
notification bell so that you know when
I come out with a new video. To check out

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:42.009
Jeremy's tutorial for his boomerang you
can click this little card here in the

00:11:42.009 --> 00:11:45.190
upper right and I'll place the link in
the video description below. After you

00:11:45.190 --> 00:11:48.100
throw the ninja star boomerang a couple
times you might notice it starts to get

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:51.819
a little bent or it might not come back
as well. What you need to do after every

00:11:51.819 --> 00:11:55.630
couple throws is just flatten it out and
reinforce the creases to make it flight

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:58.870
great again. If you find when you throw
the boomerang that it hits the ground or

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.930
it doesn't come back all the way or even
if it shoots off in the other direction

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:07.180
what you can do is hold these four boxes
on the bottom and tilt the wings up like

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:10.720
this ever so slightly and you should
notice that the boomerang will come back

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:13.180
a little better. With some practice,
throwing and catching it you'll

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:16.990
definitely become a ninja star boomerang
pro in no time. As always thanks so much

00:12:16.990 --> 00:12:25.540
for the support I'll see you soon!

